ubclass's built-in value; a bound method of a Python"] [100 2 "// function is called by pushing its frame"] [132 1 "// dictArgs are a keyword dictionary as a call's trailing keyword arguments."] [219 20 "// a dict subclass's __setitem__ sees the body's names (PY5e, part 2b)"] [250 1 "// updateBases resolves __mro_entries__ (PEP 560): the same tuple when no base has one."] [291 1 "// calculateMetaclass is _PyType_CalculateMetaclass: the most derived of meta and the bases' types."] [308 1 "// ---- type.__new__, type.__init__, type.__call__ ----"] [328 30 "// 3.15: type() takes a frozendict's items (queue 237)"] [395 3 "// type_ready_set_dict's gh-55664"] [406 2 "// type_new_set_attrs comes before PyType_Ready: a metaclass's mro() sees __class__ set"] [413 2 "// __module__, __qualname__, __doc__"] [432 2 "// __new__ a staticmethod, __init_subclass__ and __class_getitem__ classmethods"] [441 2 "// __slots__ (type_new_slots)"] [460 32 "// type_dict_set_doc; a member named __doc__ is there already (typing's _SpecialForm)"] [462 2 "// __eq__ without __hash__ makes the class unhashable"] [470 2 "// __set_name__"] [479 4 "// type_new_set_names: _PyErr_FormatNote"] [488 2 "// __init_subclass__: super(type, type), whose check reads the MRO (a custom mro() may have left the class out)"] [510 1 "// checkLayouts refuses bases whose instance layouts conflict."] [521 1 "// bestBase is best_base: the base whose solid base is the most derived."] [539 1 "// c3MRO is the C3 linearization of t over its bases (mro_internal's mro_implementation)."] [601 1 "// mangle is _Py_Mangle: __x in class C is _C__x."] [624 1 "// ---- object.__new__, object.__init__ ----"] [626 1 "// overrides is a heap class of t's MRO defining name, or, for __new__, t's built-in solid base not"] [627 1 "// object (a built-in type's inherited slot cannot be told from its own: Go's functions do not compare)."] [638 4 "// a static type's tp_name is its module's and its name (select.poll)"] [684 25 "// its __del__ at its death (finalize.go, queue 218)"] [703 2 "// The data model's slots of object and type (REQUEST to PY5b: leave these to class.go)."] [716 1 "// ---- the slots of a class (fixup_slot_dispatchers, update_slot) ----"] [722 1 "// pyDefined is name defined by a heap class of t's MRO (a Python method), and its value."] [731 1 "// fixupSlots fills t's slots: the built-in solid base's (unwrapping a built-in subclass's value),"] [732 1 "// then a dispatcher for each special method a class of the MRO defines. Rerun on a class's"] [733 1 "// special attribute's assignment, for it and its subclasses."] [744 21 "// a custom mro() without object (typeNew refuses such a class afterwards)"] [759 28 "// bytearray's str is its repr"] [763 34 "// list___init__ and set_init ask the class of the instance"] [766 34 "// deque_iter: dequeiter_reduce gives the instance back"] [769 4 "// dict's subscript sees the subclass's instance (its __missing__; dict's accessors take the"] [770 4 "// instance through BuiltinValueHook): PY5e, part 2b"] [852 6 "// _PyObject_MaybeCallSpecialOneArg: a descriptor's AttributeError reads as no such method"] [907 4 "// slot_tp_call's _Py_EnterRecursiveCall (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's"] [908 4 "// test_recursive_call, A.__call__ = A(), overflowed Go's stack)"] [1077 1 "// reprOfInstance are the built-in types whose repr names the instance's own type (_PyType_Name(Py_TYPE(self)):"] [1078 1 "// deque's, defaultdict's): their subclasses' instances reach the Repr slot as they are, not unwrapped (PY7: a"] [1079 1 "// subclass's repr named the base)."] [1082 1 "// unwrapSlots makes a built-in base's slots work on its subclass's instances: each argument that is"] [1083 1 "// such an instance replaced by its value, and the base's __new__'s value wrapped in the instance."] [1107 16 "// an iterator's own: the instance, not its value (iter(e) is e)"] [1158 1 "// wrapNew is a built-in __new__ called for a class deriving from it: its value in an instance."]